{"event_type":"finding-event","id":"f6ab2762cdcfe476a17249dfa7cbfb851f3e450be5f5bf5cb339c8086b281d4c","occurred_at":"2026-11-21T14:46:59Z","payload":{"action":"confirmed","actor":"crq-triage/opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash","evidence":{"anchor_verified":true,"failure_class":"evidence","mapped_intervals":[[222,223]],"mapped_path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-feasibility.py","quoted_text":"        \"-drive\", \"file=%s,if=virtio,format=qcow2\" % (run / \"overlay.qcow2\"),\n        \"-drive\", \"file=%s,if=virtio,format=raw,readonly=on\" % (run / \"seed.iso\"),","reason":"`qemu_command` resolves an arbitrary run path and interpolates it directly into QEMU's comma-delimited `-drive` option. QEMU treats embedded commas as option separators unless doubled, so a state path such as `probe,local` makes `file=...` truncate or misparse and VM launch fails. This is an ordinary correctness defect in the existing command builder; no contract clause is needed.","target":"19b47d081722fc7e68640a8ea2ca00f5c230b38f"},"finding_id":"9b642ae652878daefd8f448658e4ed6ac5edf599d989d795ceb782a903115568","previous_event_id":"ba58d0b058e9d6e2b7b76248860f59a74e33c3183c3017b1c297bb6b8f911124","review_id":"f1b5131645f96822be0f07c1707f2cbcab3333693f6cab11de508eb6e932b92d"},"schema":"cq.review-ledger/v1","source_key":"finding:9b642ae652878daefd8f448658e4ed6ac5edf599d989d795ceb782a903115568:5290bd06df64635290562e5d6a3b458ac748b473ce357015ef0b962c0e7c2560"}